WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.800
An online store runs on apps that bill
by the order, the contact and the month.

2
00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:11.720
Shopify, Klaviyo, ShipBob, Gorgias,
Recharge, and the list keeps growing.

3
00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:16.620
Connexcy puts every contract and invoice
in one place, and pulls out what each one

4
00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:22.670
costs, when it renews, and how much notice
it needs. A person checks every one.

5
00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:27.570
Your ShipBob warehouse agreement renews
October 1, with 90 days' notice.

6
00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:31.890
That's peak season. So Connexcy alerts
your head of operations in April,

7
00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:33.820
while there's time to get quotes.

8
00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:36.880
Every invoice is matched to its contract.

9
00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:40.440
When your Klaviyo list grows past
your plan and the bill jumps a tier,

10
00:00:40.490 --> 00:00:44.530
it's flagged, so you can clean
the list or approve the increase.

11
00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:49.270
Before Gorgias renews, compare it with
other help desks, and see who chose it last

12
00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:54.600
time, and why. Then the renewal goes to
your finance lead, and then the founder.

13
00:00:55.210 --> 00:00:58.880
Connexcy for e-commerce
brands. Every contract.

14
00:00:58.930 --> 00:01:03.730
Every invoice. Connected. Join
the beta at connexcy.com.
